{
  "description": "Image requests the native artwork fetch sends (T3-11, docs/specs/T3-11.md, \"The fetch\"). Each vector is an ArtworkRequest { itemId, type, tag, width } with width the drawn width in canvas px. `cappedWidth` is what ArtworkRequest.cappedWidth(type, width) answers: null for a type outside Primary, Backdrop, Thumb and Logo or a width below 1, else the width capped at 400 for Primary and 1920 for the other types. `expected` is the request ArtworkFetch.prepare sends, as a path under the session's base path and the query pairs in order, or null when prepare refuses and sends nothing: an item id of 1 to 64 and a tag of 1 to 128 RFC 3986 unreserved characters, one of the four types, a width of at least 1, and a path RequestPath.isSafe accepts. Read by modules/session/android/src/test/java/dev/octave/session/http/ArtworkRequestVectorsTest.kt; a Swift loader is held to the same file. No id or tag here is a real server's.",
  "caps": {
    "Primary": 400,
    "Backdrop": 1920,
    "Thumb": 1920,
    "Logo": 1920
  },
